commit b52839f04d91d79b5716c2690ba7f76de990453e
Author: Andrew Deason <adeason@sinenomine.net>
Date:   Tue May 19 15:45:49 2026 -0500

    LINUX: Grab unixuser refs in osi_proc.c
    
    In order to implement the 'unixusers' /proc pseudo-file, osi_proc.c
    contains code to iterate over unixusers. The uu_*() functions are
    seq_operations callbacks that are called approximately like this
    pseudocode:
    
        p = uu_start();
        while (p != NULL) {
            uu_show(p);
            p = uu_next(p);
        }
        uu_stop(p);
    
    Since commit 89b22dfe86 (libafs: Implement unixuser RW locks) in OpenAFS
    1.7.1, uu_show() drops the ref for the current unixuser 'tu' before
    acquiring afs_xuser. If 'tu' is freed while we're waiting for afs_xuser,
    we'll dereference freed memory when uu_next() examines tu->next to get
    the next unixuser.
    
    Change osi_proc.c to grab and release unixuser refs while traversing
    unixusers, like we did for other files in change I849132fc08 (afs:
    Introduce and use afs_UserScan()).
    
    In uu_start(), this simply involves using afs_UserScan(), but in other
    callers, grab the refs manually, since we iterate over unixusers one at
    a time instead of directly via a for() loop.
    
    In uu_next(), also acquire AFS_GLOCK(), since we are now manipulating
    tu->refCount for various users.
    
    FIXES 135623
    
    Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.openafs.org/16833
