commit e5e639568946a10ca256a645417c3f9c69b095dd
Author: Koustubh Mattikalli <koustubh.mattikalli@ibm.com>
Date:   Sun May 24 08:54:00 2026 +0530

    log: Optimize token unlogging by cell name
    
    Use new API function ktc_ForgetTokensByCell() introduced in Change-Id
    "Ia3f3767adeb52ee357b19aec337870d99cb2e33b".
    This function allows forgetting tokens for a specific cell without
    affecting tokens for other cells.
    
    This simplifies the unlog implementation by eliminating the need of
    listing all tokens, forget them all, and then re-register all except
    those specified by the -cell option. However, the old implementation of
    forgetting and re-registering tokens is still run if the kernel does
    not support the ktc_ForgetTokensByCell() operation. The old code path
    will be removed later in a future commit.
    
    This change reduces code complexity and improves performance by
    avoiding unnecessary token listing and re-registration operations.
    
    Co-authored-by: Kailas S Zadbuke <kailashsz@in.ibm.com>
    Co-authored-by: Amar Bhandari <amar.bhandari@ibm.com>
